<title>UK: Pakistan sets $150 mln PCTL-exchangeable bond. [CORRECTED 09:25 GMT]</title>
<headline>Pakistan sets $150 mln PCTL-exchangeable bond. [CORRECTED 09:25 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects abbreviation in headline for Pakistan Telecommunications Co Ltd to PCTL from Paktel)</p>
<p>Pakistan has launched a $150 million five-year bond exchangeable into &quot;A&quot; shares of Pakistan Telecommunication Co Ltd, joint lead managers Nomura and UBS said on Thursday.</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	COUPON     6.0	 MATURITY    26.FEB.02</p>
<p> TYPE   EXCHANGEABLE  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    26.FEB.97</p>
<p>(Corrects payment date from 25.FEB.97)</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	PREMIUM    10.78 PCT PAY-FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> NOTES	PUT OPTION MAR.2000 AT 104.71, 3-YEAR NON-HARD CALL</p>
<p> SUBJECT TO 133 PCT HURDLE. STRIKE PRICE 38 RUPEES, FOREX 40.08</p>
<p> RUPEES/USD. $25 MLN GREENSHOE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
